@startuml char-compaction-flow
' ============================================================================
' char-compaction-flow.puml — PersistentARTrieChar::compact() reclaims the dead
' space incremental checkpointing accumulates, by rebuilding a dense image of the
' live term set and atomically swapping it in. Enumeration uses the FAULTING
' overlay reader, so evicted (Child::OnDisk) terms are recovered — compaction is
' correct even on an evicted trie. It is NOT RAM-bounded (materializes the live
' set), so it is an explicit maintenance op guarded by a post-enumeration RAM check.
' Source: §3 of checkpoint-growth-sequential-sibling-fixes.md.
' Color key: teal overlay/live, indigo dense image/checkpoint, blue disk/rename,
' red the RAM guard, green success.
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1.3
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #37474F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #37474F

title PersistentARTrieChar::compact() — dense-rebuild file-rewrite compaction

start
#B2DFDB:**Enumerate** live (term, value) set\niter_prefix_with_values("") — FAULTS Child::OnDisk;
note right
  Faulting reader recovers EVICTED terms,
  so compaction never drops them. self.len()
  (resident-only count) is NOT the oracle.
end note
:serialize each value → build `expected` snapshot\naccumulate <latex>live\\_data\\_bytes</latex>;
if (<latex>4 \\times live\\_data\\_bytes > </latex> available RAM ?) then (yes)
  #FFCDD2:**fail loud** — InvalidOperation\n(compaction is NOT RAM-bounded);
  stop
else (no)
endif
#C5CAE9:**Rebuild** a fresh dense trie at <name>.compacting\ninsert every (term, value) → checkpoint();
if (verify_after_compact ?) then (yes)
  #C5CAE9:**Verify by reopen** — reopened (term→value)\nmap must equal `expected`;
  if (mismatch ?) then (yes)
    #FFCDD2:fail — CheckpointVerificationFailed\n(clean up temp);
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
else (no)
endif
#BBDEFB:**Atomic finalize** (in-place):\nstash <name>.wal → .compacting-stale\nrename .compacting → <name>\nreopen self onto the dense image;
note right
  Crash before rename ⇒ the reopen
  recovery finalizer rolls back
  (restore stashed WAL, drop temp).
end note
#C8E6C9:return CompactionStats\n(terms, before/after bytes, space saved);
stop

@enduml
